# Infra and state locality

Prefer self-contained, per-repo solutions over machine-global or shared state.

When designing infra (test concurrency, locks, caches, coordination), do **not**
introduce folders or state that live outside the repo or are shared across
clones. Cap resources per-repo with a static knob instead.

Multiple clones of a repo are already independent, so cross-repo parallelism is
effectively free — favor a small per-repo cap over a shared coordinator.

The one exception is a genuinely machine-wide resource that per-repo caps can't
bound: iOS simulator RAM. Test simulators take slots from the opt-in
simulator-slots pool (`AGENTS.md > Simulator slots`), which is off wherever its
master doesn't exist and is crash-safe (kernel-released locks, no daemon). Keep
any future exception to that bar.
